ord"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " These are words you use to talk about injuries."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to be laid up"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to be unable to move due to injury"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Aunt Nelly was laid up for weeks."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le03ob06aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "Hooray! "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "used to express joy and excitement"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Hooray! A strike!"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le03ob06aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to get injured"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to hurt yourself physically"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Someone always gets injured."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le03ob06aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to lean"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to balance of weight on someone or something"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Lean on me and I'll lean on you."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le03ob06aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "shooting pain"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a pain that is intense"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": " Example: I have a shooting pain going up my leg."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le03ob06aud06"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "The Second Conditional - Talking About Hypothetical Situations"}, {"type": "describer", "content": " You use the second conditional to talk about unreal or imaginary (hypothetical) situations in the future."}, {"type": "text", "content": "For example:<br/><span class=\"italic\">If I had a million dollars, I would buy a car</span>."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Do you have a million dollars?  No.<br/> Is it possible to suddenly get a million dollars? Not really.<br/>What would you do if you had a million dollars? Buy a car."}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use the Simple Past verb + <span class=\"italic\">would</span>"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":5,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"IF\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Conditional\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Result\\\"}\",\"\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"simple past \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"would + base verb\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"If\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"I married Peter,\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"I would be happy.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"If\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"it snowed next July,\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"I would be very surprised.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"If\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"I were you,\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"I would be jumping up and down.\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Remember to use a comma (,) after the IF clause. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "In conversation, it is common to use contractions. (I would = I'd)."}, {"type": "example", "content": "If I were you, I'd be jumping up and down."}, {"type": "example", "content": "I'd get that checked out if I were you."}, {"type": "example", "content": "If we went home, we'd need to have some movies to watch."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Giving Advice"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use modals to give advice. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "The most common modals for giving advice are:<br/><span class=\"italic\"> should</span>, <span class=\"italic\">ought to</span> and <span class=\"italic\">had better</span>."}, {"type": "text", "content": "You can think of modals as \u201chelping verbs\u201d. They add meaning to the main verb of a sentence. In this case, these modals add the meaning of advice. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\"> Should</span> is the most common modal used to give advice. <br/> <span class=\"italic\"> Ought to</span> and <span class=\"italic\"> had better</span>  are used for giving strong advice."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":4,\"columns\":4,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Subject\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Modal\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Main Verb\\\"}\",\"\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"You\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"should\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"get\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"moving.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"We\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"ought to\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"go\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"home and relax.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"You\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"had better\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"sit\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"down.\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}, {